   {
    "quote": "<p>Mistakes with numbers can have a cascading effect for investigative stories, and a damaging effect for audience trust, as many other erroneous figures, trend claims, and conclusions can flow from that initial error.</p>",
    "url": "https://journalistsresource.org/home/10-simple-data-errors-that-can-ruin-an-investigation/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "<p>In a summary echoed by other experts, Sahejpal says avoiding mistakes generally involves asking yourself three questions: Do you actually have the full dataset? Have you spoken to the person behind the data to know what it really means? And what does the data <em>not</em> tell you?</p>",
    "url": "https://journalistsresource.org/home/10-simple-data-errors-that-can-ruin-an-investigation/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "<p>Still, mistakes do happen, and here are 10 common causes, according to data journalism experts.</p>",
    "url": "https://journalistsresource.org/home/10-simple-data-errors-that-can-ruin-an-investigation/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "<p>“If you have a dataset of perfectly 1,000 or 10,000 rows, I would bet money something is off,” Sahejpal says. “And I can’t tell you the number of students I’ve had who downloaded a file, and didn’t realize they’d downloaded a filtered version. Another mistake is if you don’t check that the range of your dataset is equal to the reported range on a government website.”</p>",
    "url": "https://journalistsresource.org/home/10-simple-data-errors-that-can-ruin-an-investigation/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "<p>“The number one thing I do to avoid mistakes as an editor is to list what the data doesn’t tell you,” he says. “What we call the ‘limitations section’ on your dataset is your strongest ally, because if you know what it doesn’t tell you, you know to not say what you should not say, and what further questions to ask.”</p>",
    "url": "https://journalistsresource.org/home/10-simple-data-errors-that-can-ruin-an-investigation/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
   {
    "quote": "<p>“Not paying attention to the top left corner is the easiest mistake you will make, and it can end careers,” warns Thompson. “You want to always keep your data tied to other lines and rows, so you need to highlight the whole kit-and-caboodle. Don’t ever sort only a single column; always use the top left hand corner — it should be like tying your shoes.”</p>",
    "url": "https://journalistsresource.org/home/10-simple-data-errors-that-can-ruin-an-investigation/",
    "pass": 3,
    "first_seen": "2026-11-06"
   },
